# interplay_diff_segment_split: The Workload (inc_k dispatches and blit copies whose results depend on their order) in six encodings, each into its own buffer: one segment per run of an encoder type; one segment per step; runs as chains of continued segments (continuesPrevious/continuedByNext, one encoder, the pipeline set once); each step its own exec, rung together; the steps split across two execs mid-run; and the first encoding on a child FIFO. All six agree (each range holds one segment, docs/testing.md section 6.12).
